{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795713032,"nonce":"QGMciUqQTlYAgCF4vTm92fcqA/w=","title":"The adaptive L-shape tutorial calls jno.solve.enrich() without its required criterion= and crashes","message":"The tutorial script adaptive_l_shape.py (docs/tutorial_examples/08_fem_and_varpinns) stops at the p-adaptivity step with a TypeError, so the tutorial cannot be run end to end.\n\n**What goes wrong.** The script calls `jno.solve.enrich(theta=0.8, max_iters=5)` (p run) and `jno.solve.enrich(theta=0.8, max_iters=4)` (hp run). `enrich` has a required keyword-only argument `criterion`, because it deliberately ships no built-in estimator (the docstring explains the Zienkiewicz-Zhu estimator cannot see the enriched space and was measured to be anti-correlated with the error). Observed: `TypeError: enrich() missing 1 required keyword-only argument: 'criterion'`. Expected: the tutorial runs and prints its h / r / p / hp comparison. The tutorial's prose and its module docstring describe enrichment as if it had a default marking rule.\n\n**Reproduce.**\n\n    python docs/tutorial_examples/08_fem_and_varpinns/adaptive_l_shape.py\n\nor just `jno.solve.enrich(theta=0.8, max_iters=5)`, which raises at once. Checked on main; the same two calls are present on the branch that rewrites this file (the calls there also lack criterion=).\n\n**Expected.** Both calls pass a criterion, for example the gradient magnitude used in the enrich docstring, `criterion=jno.np.sqrt(ui.x**2 + ui.y**2)` with `ui` the bound solution of the tutorial's own form. The tutorial's numbers (error ratios, enriched fractions, asserts such as `0 \u003c mask_p.mean() \u003c 1`) were presumably written against an older default and have to be re-measured with the chosen criterion, and the text that quotes them updated. I did not run the script with a criterion, so I do not know whether its asserts still hold.\n\n**Where.** `docs/tutorial_examples/08_fem_and_varpinns/adaptive_l_shape.py` (the two `enrich(...)` calls and the explanation of the p and hp steps); the rendered copy `docs/tutorials/08-fem-and-varpinns/adaptive-l-shape.md`; `jno/solve.py::enrich` (signature, where criterion is required).\n\n**Workaround.** Pass `criterion=jno.np.sqrt(ui.x**2 + ui.y**2)` (the bound trial field's gradient magnitude) in both calls.\n\n**Direction.** Fix the tutorial, not the API: the refusal to guess a criterion is documented and intended. Add the criterion to both calls, rerun, update the printed comparison and the prose. Consider running the tutorial scripts in the nightly docs check, which would have caught this.","files":null}]}